\pard\sl360\slmult1\tx1136\ul\b 4\ulnone . Security Considerations\b0\par

\pard\li284\sl240\slmult1\tx1136 Any data compression method involves the reduction of redudancy in the data. Consequently, any corruption of the data is likely to have severe effects and be difficult to correct. Uncompressed text, on the other hand, will probably still be readable despite the presence of some corrupted bytes.\par
It is recommneded that systems using this data format provide some means of validating the integrity of the compressed data, such as by setting and checking CRC-32 check value.\par
\par

